-- 'EffectfulHost x a' is a @newtype@ over @Eff (BaseEffectfulHostRow x) a@
-- where the row carries every Reflex host capability upstream folds into
-- 'SpiderHost'\'s instance chain.
--
-- The two Spider engine functions that upstream expresses as
-- 'SpiderHost'-returning ('runFrame' and 'Reflex.Spider.Internal.run') are
-- REPRODUCED here as plain 'IO'-returning helpers ('frame' and 'runE'),
-- with the SpiderHost newtype wrapper stripped. Their bodies are otherwise
-- byte-for-byte ports of Spider's — same env fields, same cleanup order,
-- same recursive-frame subscribe pattern.
--
-- === 'Control.Monad.Fix.MonadFix' with Reflex recursive patterns
--
-- Effectful's @Eff@ has this @'MonadFix'@ instance:
--
-- > instance MonadFix (Eff es) where
-- >   mfix f = unsafeEff $ \\es -> mfix $ \\a -> unEff (f a) es
--
-- This delegates directly to @IO@'s 'System.IO.fixIO', which relies on
-- the underlying computation not eagerly demanding the recursive value.
-- The subtle risk: any effect interpreter that eagerly subscribes to a
-- Reflex event during its call — inside an @mfix@ / @rec@ / @mdo@ body
-- — will walk that event's graph and force references to the recursive
-- value before it's computed, throwing @cyclic evaluation in fixIO@.
--
-- The 'runHold' interpreter here uses bare 'runEventM' (not 'frame')
-- specifically to avoid this: 'frame' calls 'runHoldInits' at the end of
-- each invocation, which subscribes to all scheduled holds — walking the
-- graph and forcing recursive references during 'mfix' bodies. Bare
-- 'runEventM' lets 'SI.hold' just enqueue a 'SomeHoldInit' onto the
-- shared env's init queue; subscription happens at the next 'frame'-call
-- boundary (which is always outside the current 'mfix'). This mirrors
-- upstream 'PerformEventT's batching model, where 'runHostFrame'
-- processes all in-batch holds at once at the end of 'unPerformEventT'.
--
-- Any new interpreter that touches Reflex operations MUST maintain this
-- invariant: don't eagerly subscribe / walk event graphs within the
-- interpreter body if callers might invoke it under 'mfix'.
